# OksaSDR tour, "On the air": CW on 80 m, a QSO in Danish on 3.5233 (OY1CT spotted there on the DX cluster at 22:48 UTC),
# Autotune, the decoder's copy on the strip over the waterfall (a new run starts it empty). Receive only.
pin 5
record 15
caption !speed 3
caption # On the air
ready
wait 4000
caption !speed 1
caption CW: the CW section, and Autotune puts the signal on the pitch for the decoder.
taptext CW ~1263,82
taptext View ~1324,82
freq 3.5233
span 6
wait 1000
caption !mark 560,115
mode CW
wait 2000
tapname cwAutotune
wait 2500
caption CW on 80 m at 3.523 MHz, as it sounds; the decoder copies it on the strip over the waterfall.
wait 30000
caption -
taptext View ~1324,82
taptext CW ~1263,82
record off
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 2000
slices
